
1. Lists — The Mutable Parts Bin

While a string is an engraved nameplate (immutable), a list is a parts bin on the bench (mutable). It allows you to modify, add, remove, and reorder elements in-place.
Creation & Heterogeneous Data Types
 * Square Brackets ([]): Define a list.
 * Mixed Contents: Unlike arrays, lists can store mixed data types in a single bin.
   bin = [25.02, 24.98, 25.06]             # List of floats[span_5](start_span)[span_5](end_span)
mixed = ["PE-26-0137", 25.01, True]     # Holds str, float, and bool[span_6](start_span)[span_6](end_span)

